IO::K8s::Role::APIObject::resource_plural defaults to undef, and no shipped class overrides it. Only IO::K8s::AutoGen sets one, and only when a provider passed resource_plural explicitly in its resource_map entry (AutoGen.pm:184). fetch_resource_map in Kubernetes::REST maps Kind -> class path and never supplies a plural.

Measured against 1.107 (resource_map_from_cluster => 0):

    Pod           -> IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod            resource_plural=(undef)
    Deployment    -> IO::K8s::Api::Apps::V1::Deployment     resource_plural=(undef)
    Ingress       -> IO::K8s::Api::Networking::V1::Ingress  resource_plural=(undef)
    NetworkPolicy -> ...::Networking::V1::NetworkPolicy     resource_plural=(undef)
    Endpoints     -> IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Endpoints      resource_plural=(undef)

Why it matters: RBAC speaks plurals (pods, deployments), the API speaks Kinds (Pod, Deployment). Anything doing authorization work needs Kind -> plural. MCP::K8s asks IO::K8s first and gets undef every time, so it falls back to its own /api/v1 + /apis discovery plus an lc+s heuristic — and a wrong plural there is indistinguishable from a denied permission.

The plural is not derivable (Endpoints -> endpoints, NetworkPolicy -> networkpolicies, Ingress -> ingresses) but it IS statically known for every built-in, the same way %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP is written out.

Options: a resource_plural class method on generated/shipped classes, or a plural lookup alongside expand_class. Either kills the heuristic in every downstream consumer.

Reported from: p5-mcp-k8s (_resource_plural tier 2).
Plurals are not being guessed: extracted from the upstream REST paths in
spec/v1.36.3.json (operations with x-kubernetes-group-version-kind and
x-kubernetes-action list|post, last non-parameterised path segment, subresource
segments filtered). 95 group|version|Kind pairs, zero ambiguity.

Coverage vs. the default resource_map: 75 of 78 short names. The 3 misses are
correct, not gaps - Eviction, Scale and TokenRequest are subresources
(pods/eviction, deployments/scale, serviceaccounts/token) and have no plural of
their own upstream. They must keep returning undef.

